WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Start with exposure. If you buy 5 shares at $40, the starting purchase amount is $200 before costs. Decide what loss you can afford.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Price can fall. A fall from $40 to $35 is a $5 loss per share, or $25 on 5 shares before any costs. Losses can be larger.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Stops have limits. A stop order becomes a market order when triggered. Its eventual execution price may be worse than the stop price.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:28.000
A stop-limit trade-off. A stop-limit order adds a limit price after the trigger, but the order might never fill if prices move past it.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Diversify thoughtfully. Putting all funds into one stock concentrates risk. Spreading exposure may reduce some risk without removing it.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Check order details. Verify buy or sell, ticker, number of shares, order type, entered prices, and the broker’s displayed estimate.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Plan for uncertainty. Prices, fees, and available liquidity can change. A plan should allow for outcomes beyond the example numbers.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Pause and summarize. State your order, expected exposure, main risk, and why the chosen order type fits your goal before submitting.
